          </h2>
          <p>
            We heard versions of the same four complaints from nearly every dishwasher owner we talked to during this project. All four are avoidable, and none of them require buying a different or more expensive machine.
          </p>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-8">
            <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-red-50 flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-red-500" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15.536 8.464a5 5 0 010 7.072m2.828-9.9a9 9 0 010 12.728M5 12h.01M8 12a4 4 0 108 0 4 4 0 00-8 0z"></path></svg>
              </div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-gray-900 mb-2">Ignoring the dB Rating</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Buyers in open-concept homes routinely choose a dishwasher on price alone, then regret it the first time it interrupts a dinner conversation or a phone call from the kitchen. A 51 dB machine is not a minor step down from a 42 dB one — it is dramatically more intrusive, and it's very hard to fix after installation without buying a new machine.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-red-50 flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-red-500" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 11H5m14 0a2 2 0 012 2v6a2 2 0 01-2 2H5a2 2 0 01-2-2v-6a2 2 0 012-2m14 0V9a2 2 0 00-2-2M5 11V9a2 2 0 012-2m0 0V5a2 2 0 012-2h6a2 2 0 012 2v2M7 7h10"></path></svg>
              </div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-gray-900 mb-2">Overloading Racks and Blocking Spray Arms</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Cramming in one extra plate or angling a large pot over the spray arm's rotation path is the single most common cause of a load coming out with food still stuck to it. Spray arms need to complete a full, unobstructed rotation. Load large items around the edges and check that the arms spin freely before starting a cycle.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-red-50 flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-red-500" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 3v2m6-2v2M9 19v2m6-2v2M5 9H3m2 6H3m18-6h-2m2 6h-2M7 19h10a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H7a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2z"></path></svg>
              </div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-gray-900 mb-2">Using the Wrong Detergent for Your Sensor System</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Machines with automatic soil sensors, like the KitchenAid ProWash or Miele AutoDos, are calibrated around specific detergent chemistry. Using a gel or off-brand pod that dissolves at the wrong rate can confuse the turbidity sensor and cause it to either under-run or over-run the cycle. Stick with the detergent type your manufacturer's manual recommends for sensor-equipped machines.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-red-50 flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-red-500" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M4 4v5h.582m15.356 2A8.001 8.001 0 004.582 9m0 0H9m11 11v-5h-.581m0 0a8.003 8.003 0 01-15.357-2m15.357 2H15"></path></svg>
              </div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-gray-900 mb-2">Skipping Filter Maintenance</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Most modern dishwashers have a removable filter at the bottom of the tub that traps food particles instead of grinding them, like older models did. Most owners don't know it exists, never clean it, and wonder why their dishwasher develops an odor or stops cleaning as well after a year or two. Pull it, rinse it under the tap, and reseat it monthly.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- FAQ -->
        <div id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6 font-sans border-b pb-4">
            Frequently Asked Questions
          </h2>
          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-xl text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the quietest dishwasher you can buy?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700">The Miele G 7566 SCVi was the quietest dishwasher in our test group at <strong>39 decibels</strong>, essentially inaudible from an adjacent room. The Bosch 800 Series was close behind at 42 dB. As a general rule, look for anything rated 44 dB or below if noise is your top priority, especially in an open-concept kitchen.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-xl text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the best budget dishwasher in 2026?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700">The <strong>Whirlpool WDT730PAHZ</strong> is the best budget dishwasher we tested. It costs meaningfully less than every other machine on our list and still delivers a competent soil sensor cycle and a useful 1-Hour Wash option, though it runs louder at 51 dB and skips a third rack.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-xl text-gray-900 mb-2">Do I really need a dishwasher with a third rack?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700">A third rack is not essential, but it meaningfully improves capacity by giving utensils, small lids, and cooking tools their own dedicated space instead of crowding the lower rack and blocking the spray arm. If you regularly run full loads or entertain, a <strong>dishwasher with a third rack</strong> is worth prioritizing. If you live alone or run small loads, it matters far less.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-xl text-gray-900 mb-2">Should I buy a panel-ready dishwasher or a standard front?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700">A <strong>panel-ready dishwasher</strong> is worth it if you want a fully built-in, custom-cabinetry look and are willing to pay for a matching panel and professional installation. A standard front finish is simpler, less expensive, and easier to replace later. Most homeowners doing a straightforward appliance swap are better served by a standard front unit.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-xl text-gray-900 mb-2">Why are my dishes still spotty after running the dishwasher?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700">Persistent spotting and film even in a well-functioning dishwasher is often caused by hard water, not the machine itself. Dissolved calcium and magnesium in your water supply leave mineral deposits on glassware and dishes and reduce how effectively detergent can work. Using rinse aid helps, but if spotting continues across multiple detergents and cycles, a <a href="/best-water-softener-system/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-bold no-underline">whole-home water softener</a> addresses the root cause.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-xl text-gray-900 mb-2">How long does a dishwasher typically last?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700">A well-maintained dishwasher typically lasts <strong>8 to 12 years</strong>, with premium brands like Miele and Maytag's warrantied models often exceeding that range. Regular filter cleaning, avoiding overloading, and using the correct detergent type for your machine's sensor system all meaningfully extend service life. Neglected maintenance is the most common reason dishwashers fail early.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

